    "description": "An exit interview routine that consolidates de-identified responses into themes and keeps the raw note in the approved repository.",
    "category": "Workforce planning",
    "publishedAt": "2026-11-11",
    "readTime": "12 min read",
    "thumbnail": "/thumbnails/november-11/hrcoordinators-prepare-an-exit-interview-summary-with-retention-themes.webp",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "The control this exit interview summary needs",
        "paragraphs": [
          "A exit interview summary queue is only useful when every item has one owner and one next action. HR Coordinators asks the team to record the case as soon as an exit interview is completed, before the file has already moved. The HR coordinator attaches the exit interview note, the theme coding list, and the confidentiality rule to the same case reference and dates each observation. A control that depends on memory fails quietly, and the failure usually appears in a later reconciliation.",
          "HR Coordinators separates a request from the decision it needs. A complete packet that contains the theme coding list and the confidentiality rule is still not an approval. The HR coordinator may mark the packet ready, but the HR business partner records the decision to publish, redact, or hold the summary. That distinction keeps preparation speed from being mistaken for authority."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "What the exit interview summary record must show",
        "paragraphs": [
          "The evidence standard for exit interview summary is deliberately modest and repeatable. Record the exit interview note, the theme coding list, and the confidentiality rule with the date each was observed. Keep the retention summary beside the correction note so a later reader can see what changed. Mark a missing value as missing instead of filling it from memory, because an invented value will be treated as fact.",
          "Sensitive exit interview summary evidence belongs in the approved repository, not in a personal folder. HR Coordinators keeps only the reference and access path in the working note and limits the theme coding list to the people who need it. The HR coordinator should not copy employee identifiers into an unapproved tool. Access to the case should end when the assignment ends."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where the coordinator's work stops",
        "paragraphs": [
          "When exit interview summary touches employee privacy or a retention report, the dependent action waits for the HR business partner. HR Coordinators records the pause reason and the time the question was raised. The HR coordinator routes the case with the exit interview note and the confidentiality rule attached instead of resolving it alone. That pause is not delay; it is the control working as designed.",
          "The HR coordinator may compare the exit interview note with the confidentiality rule and write the difference in plain language. The HR business partner decides whether the difference changes the decision to publish, redact, or hold the summary or needs a correction. HR Coordinators records the question and the answer in the same case note. Neither role should rely on an earlier verbal answer that is not attached to the file."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "The daily exit interview summary routine",
        "paragraphs": [
          "HR Coordinators keeps the exit interview summary queue small enough to finish each day. A queue that never empties hides its oldest item behind a healthy average. Each case gets one owner, one next action, and one review date tied to the retention summary. The next person should be able to continue from the exit interview note without reconstructing the day.",
          "Compare arrivals and completions for exit interview summary, not only the backlog total. If arrivals exceed completions for three days, the HR business partner needs to see the trend before it becomes a crisis. HR Coordinators records the count of cases waiting on the confidentiality rule as a separate line. That line shows whether the constraint is demand, evidence, or decision capacity."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Exceptions that should stop the case",
        "paragraphs": [
          "When a response identifies a person without consent, the dependent action stops until the HR business partner decides. Preserve both versions, record the observation time, and attach the narrow question to the theme coding list. The HR coordinator does not choose the more convenient value or rewrite the earlier record. HR Coordinators gives the exception a reason code so repeat patterns become visible.",
          "If access blocks exit interview summary, name the system, the role, and the approver. HR Coordinators records the failed attempt and the time it was raised instead of asking the HR coordinator to work around it. A shared login is not an acceptable shortcut, even when the deadline is close. The case stays open until access is granted or the owner changes the route."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "How to verify and close",
        "paragraphs": [
          "The review ends with one decision for exit interview summary. Fix the source, simplify the field, change the queue, or stop the work until the owner decides. HR Coordinators gives each change an owner and a check date tied to summaries with de-identified theme evidence. That is how a exit interview summary control improves instead of becoming another status meeting.",
          "Close exit interview summary only when the destination value in the source system, the approver, and the final check time are visible. A status label alone is not a close, and neither is a sent message. HR Coordinators compares the retention summary with the surviving value and records the result. If the destination cannot be checked, the case remains open with a named owner."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "The weekly exit interview summary handof",
        "paragraphs": [
          "A good handoff also states what would reopen a closed exit interview summary case. A late source, a corrected request, or a changed approval can all change the answer. HR Coordinators records those triggers beside the close note and keeps the retention summary attached. The next owner then knows whether to trust the record or reopen it.",
          "The handoff should name what was decided and what is still open for exit interview summary. HR Coordinators records the sample frame, the reviewer, and the criteria beside the exit interview note. A stable total can hide a growing tail, so the oldest case is always part of the discussion. Keep the prior procedure available so the next review can compare like with like."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "The monthly exit interview summary review",
        "paragraphs": [
          "The monthly review should end with one process change and one owner. HR Coordinators does not accept a review that ends with general encouragement. The team fixes the form, the source, or the queue rule, then checks summaries with de-identified theme evidence again next month. That rhythm turns exit interview summary from a recurring complaint into a managed control.",
          "Use the monthly exit interview summary review to test whether the template still matches the work. If reviewers repeatedly ask for the confidentiality rule or ignore the retention summary, the template is wrong. HR Coordinators removes unused fields and adds the missing evidence before the next sample. The goal is a record that the team can complete under pressure, not a longer form."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "Who approves a exit interview summary exception?",
        "a": "The HR business partner approves, while the HR coordinator prepares the evidence and records the stop reason."
      },
      {
        "q": "What closes a exit interview summary case?",
        "a": "A named owner, the source record, the decision, and the confirmed destination value in the theme coding list."
      }
    ],
